# Review Triage

## Directives

- Read `{{workflow-file}}` to identify the current issue. If its required `issue` field is empty, report that there is no active workflow issue and do not begin triage
- If `{{path.documents}}Reviews/<issue>.json` already exists, record its modification time before reading any source records. It is the re-review cutoff for this collation run
- Before re-collating, remove from the existing canonical inventory findings whose triage decision is `accept` or `vary`; retain all other existing findings and their recorded decisions
- Read only valid source records in `{{path.documents}}Reviews/<issue>/` whose modification time is strictly newer than the recorded canonical-inventory modification time. Do not read, add, or re-collate source material at or before that cutoff
- If no canonical inventory exists and no valid source records exist, report that there is nothing to triage and stop. If a canonical inventory exists but no source record is newer than its cutoff, retain its unresolved findings after the removal step and continue triage; if none remain, report that there is nothing to triage and stop
- Build or update one complete, stable canonical inventory at `{{path.documents}}Reviews/<issue>.json`: preserve existing source report references, versions, targets, and scopes, then add the eligible new source material; deduplicate only findings that describe the same underlying defect, and retain the strongest evidence for each unique finding
- Use the combined inventory format below. New findings begin with a pending triage object. If a canonical inventory already has recorded triage decisions, preserve its decision, variation, rationale, action, and completion state for matching findings
- When the reviewed work is a pull request, inspect existing pull-request comments only after collation. Mark matching combined findings as already flagged or add useful context in the combined inventory; do not modify source reports
- Report the created or updated canonical inventory path, then use Guide skill `just-one` to walk through every unique finding. Do not implement, format, commit, push, or discard changes during triage unless the user later explicitly confirms the collected accepted actions
- Keep handoff context `{{path.documents}}context.json` updated at meaningful milestones when present

## Combined inventory format

```json
{
  "issue": "<workflow issue>",
  "created_at": "<ISO 8601 timestamp>",
  "source_reports": [
    {"reviewer": "<agent-name>", "version": 1, "path": "Reviews/<issue>/<agent-name>.json"}
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "<combined-#>",
      "sources": [{"reviewer": "<agent-name>", "id": "<agent-#>", "version": 1, "target": "<source target>", "scope": "<source scope>"}],
      "priority": "P#",
      "target": "<finding target>",
      "scope": "<finding scope>",
      "location": {"file": "<path>", "start": 1, "end": 1},
      "description": "<short description>",
      "analysis": "<evidence and consequence>",
      "recommendation": "<specific action>",
      "triage": {
        "decision": "pending",
        "variation": null,
        "rationale": null,
        "action": null,
        "completion": "not started"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Guardrails

- Source reports are immutable independent evidence. Record user decisions only in the canonical inventory
- Set a combined finding's `target` and `scope` from its source report when they agree. When its sources differ, retain their individual target and scope values in `sources` and omit those combined-finding fields
- Do not start `just-one` until the canonical inventory is complete and stable
